# @@name@@

Local TypeScript/Hono gateway → Python/ADK sequential planner/writer workflow.
Node 20+ and Python 3.10+ are required. Commands below assume a POSIX shell.

## Install (workspace root)

```sh
npm install
python3 -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/python -m pip install -r apps/agents/requirements.txt
npm run build
```

Keep the generated npm lockfile; capture a resolved Python dependency lock for CI.
The template pins direct dependency compatibility baselines, not all transitives.

## Start (two terminals, workspace root)

Terminal 1, credential-free integration demo using the real ADK runtime:

```sh
WORKSPACE_DEMO=1 .venv/bin/adk api_server --host 127.0.0.1 --port @@adk_port@@ apps/agents
```

Terminal 2:

```sh
npm run start:web
```

For live model calls, stop terminal 1, configure `GOOGLE_API_KEY` in that
process environment, set `GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=FALSE`, and restart without
`WORKSPACE_DEMO=1`. Default model: `@@model@@`; override with `ADK_MODEL`.
Live mode runs two LLM stages and incurs provider usage. No credentials are
needed by the web process. Never send provider credentials in `/api/message`.

## Exercise

```sh
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:@@web_port@@/health
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:@@adk_port@@/list-apps
curl --fail http://127.0.0.1:@@web_port@@/api/message \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"text":"Hello polyglot"}'
```

Demo output contains `{"sessionId":"...","text":"DEMO: Hello polyglot"}`.
`/health` tests the gateway process only. `/api/message` exercises both runtimes.
Use Ctrl+C in both terminals to stop them.

## Boundary

- `apps/web/src/app.ts`: validates text-only requests, creates a fresh ADK session,
  calls `/run`, returns the last model text event. Contract: `contracts/message.schema.json`.
- `apps/agents/@@agent_name@@/agent.py`: exports `root_agent`; planner stores
  `draft` in session state, writer consumes it. The ADK app name is the folder name.
- `ADK_BASE_URL` (gateway environment) defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:@@adk_port@@`.
  It is trusted process configuration; requests cannot override it.
- `PORT` overrides the gateway's default `@@web_port@@` listener.
- Every request creates a session; this local demo has no authenticated chat
  history, persistence guarantee, or cleanup scheduler. Restart/clean up the dev
  session store as needed. Add identity binding and session lifecycle management
  before adapting it to a multi-user application.
- 400: malformed/invalid request; 413: body over 64 KiB; 502: ADK unavailable,
  failed, or returned unexpected output; 504: 60-second gateway deadline.
  A timeout does not cancel an already-running model invocation; do not auto-retry.
- The generator creates files only; it does not install tools, provision cloud
  services, or register a command with Google Agents CLI.

To add this to an existing repo, first generate into a new sibling directory,
then merge selected files with that repo's workspace/package conventions.
